        "chunk_federal_privacy_regulation_0",
        {
          "type": "chunk",
          "text": "Federal Privacy Regulation - Act Z (Data Sharing Restrictions)\nThis act governs the transfer of protected customer data containing Personally Identifiable Information (PII) by domestic corporations.\n\nSection 102 (Cross-Border Compliance):\nAll domestic corporations must comply with Federal Privacy Regulations. Section 102 strictly prohibits the sharing of protected Customer Data (including PII) with any Foreign Entities or storing such data in a Foreign Jurisdiction that lacks an established data adequacy treaty with the federal government. Foreign jurisdictions that lack adequate safeguards or",
          "source_file": "federal_privacy_regulation.txt",
          "doc_type": "text"
        }
      ],
